READ: 'depth of R_i after' is the depth in the record group of the transported record.  If it
      is 1 the permutation only relabels the records; if it is > 1 the transported record is a
      relation among the coupled ones, and whether the environment still holds it is exactly
      what the chi columns report.  The 'separate' rows are the control: there a single site
      knows one coupled record and nothing of depth > 1, so transport out of depth 1 must
      take the single-site chi to zero.
